WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.688
If an agent process disappears, task state

00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:06.849
should not disappear with it. Herdr

00:00:06.849 --> 00:00:08.957
Orchestrator places multiple coding

00:00:08.957 --> 00:00:12.118
harnesses behind one local control plane.

00:00:12.118 --> 00:00:15.279
Models may propose tasks and select

00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:18.967
workers. But Python and SQLite always own

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:22.128
the queue, leases, retries, and success

00:00:22.128 --> 00:00:25.289
decisions. Remember it this way: Herdr

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:27.923
hosts terminals, while the Coordinator

00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:29.504
owns the facts.

00:00:29.954 --> 00:00:33.687
The first step is loading a declarative

00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:37.421
workflow, not starting a model. TOML fixes

00:00:37.421 --> 00:00:39.554
concurrency, leases, timeouts, placement,

00:00:39.554 --> 00:00:43.287
and the allowed workers. The router sees

00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:47.020
only a compact harness catalog, not six

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.220
long contexts. After Droid, Grok, Codex,

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.954
Pi, Claude, or Hermes is selected, its

00:00:53.954 --> 00:00:57.687
full profile is injected at dispatch. This

00:00:57.687 --> 00:01:01.420
keeps context small and locks routing to

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.487
configured candidates.

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:06.801
After a task enters SQLite, its dedupe

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.114
key prevents duplicate work. Claim runs

00:01:10.114 --> 00:01:13.426
inside an immediate write transaction. It

00:01:13.426 --> 00:01:16.738
increments the attempt, sets the lease,

00:01:16.738 --> 00:01:20.602
chooses a replica slot, and creates a

00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:24.467
correlation ID. Each wave claims only the

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.675
configured capacity before dispatching

00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:28.883
through Herdr. Store deterministically

00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:31.643
folds outcomes into success, blocked,

00:01:31.643 --> 00:01:35.508
retry, or failure. A stale attempt can

00:01:35.508 --> 00:01:38.820
never overwrite a newly claimed execution.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.816
Herdr runtime does not treat a running

00:01:42.816 --> 00:01:46.361
process as proof that a task started.

00:01:46.361 --> 00:01:49.907
It first proves the pane shell is

00:01:49.907 --> 00:01:52.946
ready, then proves the harness is

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.478
interactive. Before submitting the prompt,

00:01:55.478 --> 00:01:59.024
it records the state change sequence. Only

00:01:59.024 --> 00:02:02.570
a strict sequence advance proves a new

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:06.115
turn. The turn must then stabilize in

00:02:06.115 --> 00:02:09.154
idle or done. Blocked, working, unknown,

00:02:09.154 --> 00:02:12.700
and timeout are not success. Every wait

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.726
shares one bounded deadline.

00:02:15.176 --> 00:02:18.220
After choosing a worker, the system

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.770
chooses where the task runs. A tab

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.307
provides a dedicated visible location.

00:02:24.307 --> 00:02:27.858
Pane placement shares a tab within one

00:02:27.858 --> 00:02:30.394
wave while preserving separate terminals.

00:02:30.394 --> 00:02:33.438
Worktree placement creates a task branch,

00:02:33.438 --> 00:02:36.481
checkout, and Herdr workspace for write

00:02:36.481 --> 00:02:39.017
work. Explicit overrides and worker

00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:41.554
defaults come first. Deterministic read

00:02:41.554 --> 00:02:44.597
and write signals come next. Only

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.641
ambiguous cases reach a bounded topology

00:02:47.641 --> 00:02:50.177
controller. A worktree isolates a

00:02:50.177 --> 00:02:51.699
checkout, not security.

00:02:52.149 --> 00:02:55.957
Each of the six harnesses receives fixed

00:02:55.957 --> 00:02:58.677
maximum automation flags that planners

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:01.941
cannot override. These flags reduce local

00:03:01.941 --> 00:03:05.205
confirmations, but they do not authorize

00:03:05.205 --> 00:03:07.925
pushes, merges, publishing, or production

00:03:07.925 --> 00:03:10.645
actions. Claude workspace trust has

00:03:10.645 --> 00:03:13.909
another guard. Three stable markers must

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:17.173
appear, and the resolved execution root

00:03:17.173 --> 00:03:20.981
must match one complete output line. Login

00:03:20.981 --> 00:03:22.613
prompts, authentication, another

00:03:22.613 --> 00:03:25.333
directory, or missing markers never

00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:26.965
trigger automatic input.

00:03:27.415 --> 00:03:30.938
Settled only means the agent stopped. It

00:03:30.938 --> 00:03:34.461
does not prove the task is correct.

00:03:34.461 --> 00:03:37.984
An output receipt must appear in new

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:41.507
lines from the current turn. Prompt echoes

00:03:41.507 --> 00:03:45.031
and old output cannot count. A file

00:03:45.031 --> 00:03:48.050
receipt must stay inside the execution

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.567
root, reject absolute paths, parent

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:53.083
traversal, and symlinks, and change

00:03:53.083 --> 00:03:56.607
relative to its baseline. Failed tasks may

00:03:56.607 --> 00:03:59.626
receive more attempt budget. Blocked tasks

00:03:59.626 --> 00:04:03.149
continue on the same agent, pane, and

00:04:03.149 --> 00:04:05.666
attempt after a reviewed response.

00:04:06.116 --> 00:04:08.709
The Dashboard projects SQLite durable

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:12.858
state and Herdr runtime into one read-only

00:04:12.858 --> 00:04:15.970
snapshot. It shows queue state, attention

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:19.081
items, receipt history, and a compound

00:04:19.081 --> 00:04:22.193
project, worktree, tab, and pane topology.

00:04:22.193 --> 00:04:24.786
Structural changes trigger layout, while

00:04:24.786 --> 00:04:27.897
status changes update content only, so

00:04:27.897 --> 00:04:31.009
live refreshes remain stable. The server

00:04:31.009 --> 00:04:34.639
binds only to loopback, validates Host and

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:37.751
port, applies CSP and field allowlists,

00:04:37.751 --> 00:04:40.344
and never reads prompts, environment

00:04:40.344 --> 00:04:42.937
variables, or complete terminal output.

00:04:43.387 --> 00:04:45.466
Alongside ordinary dispatch, standardized

00:04:45.466 --> 00:04:48.065
delivery is available only through

00:04:48.065 --> 00:04:50.663
explicit opt-in. It resolves

00:04:50.663 --> 00:04:52.742
specification-blocking decisions, then

00:04:52.742 --> 00:04:55.341
creates an accepted spec and

00:04:55.341 --> 00:04:57.939
dependency-ordered ticket graph. Each

00:04:57.939 --> 00:05:01.058
ticket is implemented in an isolated

00:05:01.058 --> 00:05:04.176
worktree and closed with commit and

00:05:04.176 --> 00:05:06.255
acceptance evidence. After integration,

00:05:06.255 --> 00:05:09.893
fresh Standards and Spec reviewers run in

00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:12.492
parallel, and the controller adjudicates

00:05:12.492 --> 00:05:15.610
every finding. Repair rounds are bounded.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.728
Success stops on an isolated integration

00:05:18.728 --> 00:05:19.248
branch.

00:05:19.698 --> 00:05:23.280
This project is not an operating system

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.839
sandbox. It protects state transitions,

00:05:25.839 --> 00:05:27.885
evidence, and authorization boundaries.

00:05:27.885 --> 00:05:30.956
Model artifacts pass exact-key, enum,

00:05:30.956 --> 00:05:33.514
length, and allowlist checks. Telemetry

00:05:33.514 --> 00:05:37.096
stays local by default, exporters are off

00:05:37.096 --> 00:05:40.167
by default, and fields are sanitized

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.725
before persistence. The installer manages

00:05:42.725 --> 00:05:45.796
only manifest-owned project paths and

00:05:45.796 --> 00:05:48.866
stops conservatively on symlinks or user

00:05:48.866 --> 00:05:51.936
changes. Garbage collection starts as a

00:05:51.936 --> 00:05:55.006
dry run and requires creation, pane

00:05:55.006 --> 00:05:57.565
identity, and current ownership evidence.

00:05:58.015 --> 00:06:00.811
Unattended work enters the durable queue,

00:06:00.811 --> 00:06:03.141
where the Coordinator owns leases,

00:06:03.141 --> 00:06:05.937
retries, and receipts. Live operations use

00:06:05.937 --> 00:06:08.732
Manual Manager instead. It starts one

00:06:08.732 --> 00:06:11.528
interactive harness from a fixed policy

00:06:11.528 --> 00:06:13.858
directory inside the current Herdr

00:06:13.858 --> 00:06:16.654
session, and never pretends to provide

00:06:16.654 --> 00:06:19.450
queue semantics. The npx herdr-manager

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.246
entry point probes Grok, Codex, then

00:06:22.246 --> 00:06:25.042
Claude by default. Optional Manager Light

00:06:25.042 --> 00:06:28.304
only projects current pane and agent facts

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:31.565
into the sidebar through an owned config

00:06:31.565 --> 00:06:33.895
block and mutually exclusive metadata

00:06:33.895 --> 00:06:37.157
tokens. Its colors are not task receipts

00:06:37.157 --> 00:06:39.487
and do not own lifecycle.

00:06:39.937 --> 00:06:42.975
The version zero point one point six

00:06:42.975 --> 00:06:45.579
baseline has twenty-six reachable commits,

00:06:45.579 --> 00:06:48.183
twenty-six package Python modules, and

00:06:48.183 --> 00:06:50.787
twenty-two Python test files. Nine

00:06:50.787 --> 00:06:53.391
thousand five hundred forty-three Python

00:06:53.391 --> 00:06:55.995
test lines compared with nine thousand

00:06:55.995 --> 00:06:58.599
nine hundred sixteen package source lines

00:06:58.599 --> 00:07:01.636
gives a size ratio of about zero

00:07:01.636 --> 00:07:04.674
point nine six to one, not code

00:07:04.674 --> 00:07:06.844
coverage. Contributors run focused tests

00:07:06.844 --> 00:07:09.882
first, then just check, followed by a

00:07:09.882 --> 00:07:12.920
real doctor or read-only smoke when

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.090
needed. Remember three invariants: model

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.260
output is constrained, the Coordinator

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.864
owns state, and current execution must

00:07:19.864 --> 00:07:22.468
produce new evidence before success is

00:07:22.468 --> 00:07:22.902
accepted.
